# rule.require.get-set-gen-verbs

## .what
every domain operation and dao method uses one sanctioned prefix:
- core verbs: get · set · gen · del
- transformer prefixes: as* (cast/parse) · is* (boolean) — pure single-value shape work
exempt: contract/cli entry points, imperative commands (dispatchTask, enqueueTask), `with*` HOF wrappers

## .the core verbs
| verb | semantics | creates? | idempotent | analogy |
|---|---|---|---|---|
| get | retrieve, lookup, derive | never | yes | select |
| set | write/overwrite | yes | yes | upsert |
| gen | find-or-create | only if absent | yes | findsert |
| del | remove; no-op if absent | never | yes | delete |
- get: always getOne* or getAll*; never mutates. subtypes: lookup, compute (deterministic derivation), enumerate, assemble
- set: always overwrites; pair with a gen wrapper for data entities
- gen: checks extant first, sets if absent; use for caller-faced ops
- gen ↔ del mirror (ensure-present ↔ ensure-absent): can you gen it? can you del it?

## .transformers
- as$Noun (target names the cast: asStripeCustomer) or as$Noun1From$Noun2 (source matters)
- is$Noun for booleans
- cast* is DEPRECATED — migrate to as*

## .decision tree
modifies state? no → shape work? as*/is* · else get. yes → removes? del · preserve extant? gen · overwrite? set

## .synonyms → sanctioned
find/fetch/lookup/load/list → getOne*/getAll* · ensure/findOrCreate/create → gen · insert/create (write) → set · parse → as* · compute*/derive → getOne* · remove/delete/destroy/drop → del

## .enforcement
- operation without a sanctioned prefix = blocker
- get without One/All = blocker
- set on a data entity with no gen wrapper (unless explicit upsert) = blocker
- synonym verb in place of a sanctioned prefix = blocker
- new cast* operation = blocker
- as* forced to getOne*, or del* forced to set* = false positive
